. 
. * --- (4b) Sensitivity variants of the snow-hazard component ---
. * NOT alternative definitions of the Kohn index -- robustness on
> ly.
. * Kohn's 18in cutoff was calibrated on point station/snow-course
. * observations. snow_depth here is an ERA5-Land grid-box average
>  averaged
. * again over an entire county, and that spatial averaging remove
> s exactly
. * the local maxima an 18in cutoff is meant to catch, so wsi_snow
> _days is
. * near-zero across most of the eastern/midwestern deer range and
. * winter_severity_index there is effectively wsi_cold_days alone
>  (see
. * open item 1 in the header for the measured 1980-81 numbers). T
> hese
. * lower-threshold indices let that be shown in a robustness tabl
> e rather
. * than asserted. Report winter_severity_index as the headline me
> asure.
. foreach thr in 12 8 {
  2.     capture confirm variable days_snow_depth_`thr'in_m1
  3.     if _rc {
  4.         di as text "NOTE: days_snow_depth_`thr'in_m1 not foun
> d -- wsi_snow_days_`thr'in and winter_severity_index_snow`thr' s
> et to missing."
  5.         gen wsi_snow_days_`thr'in = .
